From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 13:29:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] node-executor: add application-declared local pools

Allow root Node action modules to request a bounded named local executor pool through paired source directives. Carry the required pool-bearing environment and explicit pool metadata through bundling, deployment comparison, archives, durable source and module records, and execution requests. Validate agreement at each boundary so unsupported runtimes reject the requirement instead of falling back to the default executor.

Load the committed topology at startup and reconcile it only after successful deployment commits. Route requests through lazy named LocalNodeExecutor slots, replace generations when their source, effective environment, or committed membership changes, and wait for affected predecessors to terminate and reap before constructing replacements. Preserve older count-only records conservatively and retire the default generation at the transition to exact membership.

Validate pool names, distinct-name limits, and total host RSS planning before deployment and at startup. Keep ordinary Node actions on the default executor, expose bounded pool-scoped lifecycle and topology observability, and document activation and rollback for self-hosted operators.

Add focused coverage for directive and metadata validation, archive and durable-record consistency, topology ordering and reconciliation, predecessor barriers, generation reuse and replacement, shutdown interaction, startup budgets, and metric label lifecycle.
